.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_DECAPSULATE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_decapsulate_init ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_auth_decapsulate_init ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_decapsulate
.Nd Key decapsulation using a KEM algorithm with a private key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_decapsulate_init
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const OSSL_PARAM params[]"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_auth_decapsulate_init
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *authpub"
.Fa "const OSSL_PARAM params[]"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_decapsulate
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "unsigned char *unwrapped"
.Fa "size_t *unwrappedlen"
.Fa "const unsigned char *wrapped"
.Fa "size_t wrappedlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_decapsulate_init
function initializes a private key algorithm context
.Fa ctx
for a decapsulation operation and then sets the
.Em params
on the context in the same way as calling
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3 .
Note that
.Fa ctx
usually is produced using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey 3 ,
specifying the private key to use.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_auth_decapsulate_init
function is similar to
.Fn EVP_PKEY_decapsulate_init
but also passes an
.Fa authpub
authentication public key that is used during decapsulation.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_decapsulate
function performs a private key decapsulation operation using
.Fa ctx .
The data to be decapsulated is specified using the
.Fa wrapped
and
.Fa wrappedlen
parameters (which must both non-NULL).
.Pp
The
.Fa wrapped
parameter is an output argument, to which the decapsulated shared secret
is written.
The shared secret may not match the peer's value even when decapsulation
returns success.
Instead, the shared secret must be used to derive a key that is used to
authenticate data subsequently received from the peer.
If
.Fa unwrapped
is NULL then the size of the output shared secret buffer is written to
.Em *unwrappedlen
and no decapsulation is performed, this makes it possible to determine
the required buffer size at run time.
Otherwise, the decapsulated secret data is written to
.Fa unwrapped
and the length of shared secret is written to
.Em *unwrappedlen .
.Pp
Note that the value pointed to by
.Fa unwrappedlen
(which must NOT be
.Dv NULL )
must be initialised to the length of
.Fa unwrapped ,
so that the call can validate it is of sufficient size to hold the
result of the operation.
.Pp
Absent detailed prior knowledge of the internals of the specific KEM
algorithm, callers SHOULD NOT assume that the returned shared secret is
necessarily of the maximum possible length.
The length returned via
.Em *unwrappedlen
SHOULD be used to determine the actual length of the output.
.Sh NOTES
After the call to
.Fn EVP_PKEY_decapsulate_init
algorithm-specific parameters for the operation may be set or modified
using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_decapsulate_init ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_auth_decapsulate_init
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_decapsulate
return 1 for success and 0 or a negative value for failure.
In particular a return value of -2 indicates the operation is not
supported by the private key algorithm.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Decapsulate data using RSA:
.Bd -literal
 #include <openssl/evp.h>

 /*
  * NB: assumes rsa_priv_key is an RSA private key,
  * and that in, inlen are already set up to contain encapsulated data.
  */

 EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx = NULL;
 size_t secretlen = 0;
 unsigned char *secret = NULL;;

 ctx = EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey(libctx, rsa_priv_key, NULL);
 if (ctx == NULL)
     /* Error */
 if (EVP_PKEY_decapsulate_init(ctx, NULL) <= 0)
     /* Error */

 /* Set the mode - only 'RSASVE' is currently supported */
 if (EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_kem_op(ctx, "RSASVE") <= 0)
     /* Error */

 /* Determine buffer length */
 if (EVP_PKEY_decapsulate(ctx, NULL, &secretlen, in, inlen) <= 0)
     /* Error */

 secret = OPENSSL_malloc(secretlen);
 if (secret == NULL)
     /* malloc failure */

 /* Decapsulated secret data is secretlen bytes long */
 if (EVP_PKEY_decapsulate(ctx, secret, &secretlen, in, inlen) <= 0)
     /* Error */
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_encapsulate 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KEM-RSA 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KEM-X25519 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KEM-EC 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KEM-ML-KEM-512 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KEM-ML-KEM-768 7 ,
.Xr EVP_KEM-ML-KEM-1024 7
.Sh HISTORY
The functions
.Fn EVP_PKEY_decapsulate_init
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_decapsulate
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The function
.Fn EVP_PKEY_auth_decapsulate_init
was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
.Pp
Support for
.Sy ML-KEM
was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
